window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-27e0fbf570961bc8"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"turn-an-issue-into-a-tested-pull-request\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">将问题单转化为经过测试的拉取请求</h1> <p>交付一项小型功能，并附上验收标准和审核证据。</p> <p>为 Codex 提供范围明确的问题单、已准备好的云端环境和清晰的检查项。交付实现、测试、文档和一项可供审核的变更，并为每项验收标准提供证据。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>实现范围明确的 API 问题单的初创团队工程师。</li> <li>需要同时审核实现和验证证据的审核者。</li> <li>已有验收标准和可用测试环境的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">起步提示词</h2> <p>实现一个范围明确的问题单</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">针对 [issue ID and title]，在 [repository] 的 [base branch and commit] 上，使用为此任务选定并准备好的云端环境进行实现。\n\n输入资料包：[paste or attach the issue, acceptance criteria, relevant\nfiles, public success/error schemas, authorization and pagination contract,\ntest fixtures, and approved validation commands]。\n代码库指引：[AGENTS.md and any relevant nested instructions]。\n范围：[files or component boundaries]。\n不在范围内：[explicit exclusions]。\n必需检查：[focused tests, relevant regression tests, type check,\nlint, and any required CI checks]。\n交付内容：[create a draft PR in this repository if the available integration\nsupports it and I authorize it here / return a diff and draft PR description]。\n\n首先阅读指引和相关代码。确认起始提交，并使用此环境中可用的执行工具运行现有基线检查。将所有需要新建的测试文件记录为待创建项目。\n如果基线检查失败、缺少访问权限，或必需检查无法运行，应先准确报告阻碍，再开始实现。\n\n说明简短计划，然后实施满足验收标准的最小改动。遵循现有的身份验证、错误处理、分页和测试模式。添加能区分所需行为与旧行为的测试。对于此分页示例，应要求覆盖跨页边界的相同时间戳、受限的遍历和固定夹具重放、部分及正好填满的最后一页、游标验证前的授权、无效游标情况，以及成功/错误模式检查。更新受影响的 API 文档，使其与实际实现的公开响应完全一致。\n\n实施后再次运行必需检查。针对每项验收标准，指出验证它的测试或其他证据。记录命令、结果、受测提交或工作树状态，以及未运行的检查。区分既有失败和新失败。\n绝不要把未运行的检查描述为通过。\n\n交付差异或经授权的草稿 PR、简明变更摘要、验收标准证据表、剩余风险和审核者需要采取的操作。不要合并、部署、使用生产数据、更改权限、添加依赖项或扩大约定范围。如果契约与代码库冲突，或工作需要修改模式，请停下来请求决定。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/issue-to-tested-pr/sample.zip\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">下载可运行示例（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">云端环境</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9563acffd5862bcd\">保持文档更新</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面的 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>给 Codex 一个规模较小、定义清楚的问题单，并要求它完成队友可以审核的改动：实现、测试、文档，以及证明所需行为有效的证据。请在一个已准备好的云端环境中完成任务，这样代码和验证使用的是同一套代码库环境。</p> <ol> <li> <p>在网页或桌面应用中，选择 <strong>Work in</strong> &gt; <strong>Cloud</strong>，然后选择一个已发布的环境。</p> </li> <li> <p>若要创建环境，请选择 <strong>Create environment</strong>，选择 GitHub 代码库，并让 Codex 准备运行时、依赖项和隔离的测试服务。</p> </li> <li> <p>检查设置报告、解决失败的检查，并在开始新任务前选择 <strong>Publish</strong>。</p> </li> <li> <p>请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">当前云端环境指南</a>。</p> </li> <li>请将代码库指引保存在 <a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">AGENTS.md</a> 中。</li> </ol> <p>如果依赖项或服务设置发生变化，请编辑可复用环境、测试并选择 <strong>Republish</strong>，然后在新任务中验证这些变化。</p> <p>刷新代码库不会重新运行安装或启动命令，现有任务仍会保留各自的状态。</p> <p>请单独配置所需的网络目标和测试凭据；允许访问某个目标，并不意味着已经获得该服务的访问权限。</p> <p>如果必需检查无法运行，请先完成环境设置，再使用此工作流。</p> <p><a id=\"when-to-use-it\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">适用场景</h2> <p>选择一个有书面契约、且有明确完成边界的功能，例如新增 API 端点、验证规则，或为现有服务添加小功能。问题单应能放进一个拉取请求中完成，并且其检查不需要访问生产环境。</p> <p>示例为项目活动动态添加分页。可运行的 Node.js 示例包含身份验证、项目访问权限、签名游标和现有项目详情路由。它使用内存中的固定测试记录，因此无需数据库或外部服务即可检查分页契约。</p> <p><a id=\"try-the-runnable-sample\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">试用可运行示例</h2> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/issue-to-tested-pr/sample.zip\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">下载示例（需联网）</a>，解压后打开其中的 <code>issue-to-tested-pr</code> 文件夹。请使用 <strong>Node 22.6 或更高版本</strong>。示例只使用标准库，无需安装软件包或 API 密钥。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">node --version\nnode api.mjs\nnode test.mjs --seeded\nnode test.mjs\nnode reproduce.mjs ./evidence\n</code></pre> <p><code>node api.mjs</code> 会启动本地 HTTP 服务器、请求第一页、打印公开 ID，然后关闭服务器。</p> <p><code>--seeded</code> 测试运行会故意以非零状态退出：仅按时间戳续页会漏掉第一页边界处两个时间相同的事件。改为使用“时间戳和 ID”组成的元组续页后，同一组测试会通过。</p> <p>只有在植入缺陷的状态下测试失败、而修正后的状态通过时，复现命令才算成功。</p> <p>修正后的遍历设置 <code>limit=2</code>，会在三次请求中返回以下页面：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">[evt_105, evt_104]\n[evt_103, evt_102]\n[evt_101]\n</code></pre> <p>前两页会有后续游标；最后一页的 <code>next_cursor: null</code>。</p> <p>植入缺陷的状态先返回 <code>[evt_105, evt_104]</code>，然后返回 <code>[evt_101]</code>，从而漏掉 <code>evt_103</code> 和 <code>evt_102</code>。</p> <p>成功运行时，修正后的状态会通过全部 36 项测试。植入缺陷的状态会有三项断言失败，揭示分页缺陷。</p> <p>要验证环境，请把文件放入选定的代码库，准备并发布一个具有受支持 Node 运行时的环境，然后在新的 Cloud 任务中运行命令并记录结果。</p> <p><code>reproduce.mjs</code> 会在指定证据目录中保存 <code>red.log</code>、<code>green.log</code>、<code>observed-http.json</code> 和 <code>run-manifest.json</code>。清单会记录运行时、命令、退出码、植入的缺陷、修复情况和源文件 SHA-256。</p> <p>它不会记录会话令牌或签名密钥。请阅读 <code>README.md</code> 和 <code>openapi.json</code>，了解示例的设置和公开契约。</p> <p><a id=\"inspect-the-runnable-sample\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">检查可运行示例</h3> <p>以下片段来自下载包中的文件。解压 ZIP 后请运行完整文件。</p> <details> <summary>游标和排序实现</summary> <pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">export function createApi({\n  sessions,\n  projects,\n  events,\n  signingKey,\n  seededBug = false,\n}) {\n  return createServer((request, response) =&gt; {\n    const send = (status, body) =&gt; {\n      response.writeHead(status, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n      response.end(JSON.stringify(body));\n    };\n    const fail = (code) =&gt; {\n      const [status, message] = errors[code];\n      send(status, { error: { code, message } });\n    };\n    // Authenticate, then authorize. Malformed parameters must not change these results.\n    const authorization = request.headers.authorization ?? \"\";\n    const bearer = /^Bearer ([A-Za-z0-9_-]+)$/.exec(authorization);\n    const tenantId = bearer ? sessions.get(bearer[1]) : undefined;\n    if (!tenantId) return fail(\"unauthenticated\");\n\n    const url = new URL(request.url ?? \"/\", \"http://127.0.0.1\");\n    const route = /^\\/v1\\/projects\\/([^/]+)(\\/events)?$/.exec(url.pathname);\n    let projectId;\n    try {\n      projectId = route ? decodeURIComponent(route[1]) : undefined;\n    } catch {\n      return fail(\"not_found\");\n    }\n    const project = projectId ? projects.get(projectId) : undefined;\n    if (\n      request.method !== \"GET\" ||\n      !project ||\n      project.tenant_id !== tenantId\n    ) {\n      return fail(\"not_found\");\n    }\n    // Existing project-detail behavior remains independent of pagination parameters.\n    if (!route[2]) return send(200, { id: projectId, name: project.name });\n\n    const rawLimit = url.searchParams.get(\"limit\");\n    const limit = rawLimit === null ? 25 : Number(rawLimit);\n    if (\n      url.searchParams.getAll(\"limit\").length &gt; 1 ||\n      (rawLimit !== null &amp;&amp; !/^\\d+$/.test(rawLimit)) ||\n      !Number.isInteger(limit) ||\n      limit &lt; 1 ||\n      limit &gt; 100\n    ) {\n      return fail(\"invalid_limit\");\n    }\n    let cursor;\n    if (url.searchParams.has(\"cursor\")) {\n      try {\n        if (url.searchParams.getAll(\"cursor\").length !== 1)\n          throw new Error(\"Invalid cursor\");\n        cursor = decodeCursor(\n          url.searchParams.get(\"cursor\"),\n          tenantId,\n          projectId,\n          signingKey\n        );\n      } catch {\n        return fail(\"invalid_cursor\");\n      }\n    }\n\n    const matching = events\n      .filter(\n        (event) =&gt;\n          event.tenant_id === tenantId &amp;&amp; event.project_id === projectId\n      )\n      .sort(compareEvents)\n      .filter((event) =&gt; {\n        if (!cursor) return true;\n        // Deliberate baseline defect: timestamp-only continuation loses tied rows.\n        if (seededBug)\n          return (\n            timestampValue(event.created_at) &lt; timestampValue(cursor.created_at)\n          );\n        return compareEvents(event, cursor) &gt; 0;\n      });\n    const selected = matching.slice(0, limit);\n    const items = selected.map(({ id, created_at, type, summary }) =&gt; ({\n      id,\n      created_at,\n      type,\n      summary,\n    }));\n    const nextCursor =\n      matching.length &gt; limit\n        ? encodeCursor(selected.at(-1), tenantId, projectId, signingKey)\n        : null;\n    return send(200, { items, next_cursor: nextCursor });\n  });\n}\n\nexport async function startApi(fixtures, options = {}) {\n  const server = createApi({ ...fixtures, ...options });\n  await new Promise((resolve, reject) =&gt; {\n    server.once(\"error\", reject);\n    server.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", () =&gt; resolve(undefined));\n  });\n  const address = server.address();\n  if (!address || typeof address === \"string\")\n    throw new Error(\"No listening address\");\n  return {\n    baseUrl: `http://127.0.0.1:${address.port}`,\n    close: () =&gt;\n      new Promise((resolve, reject) =&gt;\n        server.close((error) =&gt; (error ? reject(error) : resolve(undefined)))\n      ),\n  };\n}\n</code></pre> </details> <details> <summary>植入的记录和项目访问夹具</summary> <pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">export function createFixtures() {\n  const tokenA = randomBytes(24).toString(\"base64url\");\n  const tokenB = randomBytes(24).toString(\"base64url\");\n  const sessions = new Map([\n    [tokenA, \"tenant_a\"],\n    [tokenB, \"tenant_b\"],\n  ]);\n  const projects = new Map([\n    [\"feed\", { tenant_id: \"tenant_a\", name: \"Activity feed\" }],\n    [\"empty\", { tenant_id: \"tenant_a\", name: \"Empty feed\" }],\n    [\"exact\", { tenant_id: \"tenant_a\", name: \"Four events\" }],\n    [\"large\", { tenant_id: \"tenant_a\", name: \"Large feed\" }],\n    [\"precision\", { tenant_id: \"tenant_a\", name: \"Precise timestamps\" }],\n    [\"other\", { tenant_id: \"tenant_a\", name: \"Another project\" }],\n    [\"private\", { tenant_id: \"tenant_b\", name: \"Private project\" }],\n  ]);\n  const event = (id, created_at, project_id, tenant_id = \"tenant_a\") =&gt; ({\n    id,\n    created_at,\n    project_id,\n    tenant_id,\n    type: \"deployment\",\n    summary: `Synthetic event ${id}`,\n    internal_note: \"This field must never enter the HTTP response.\",\n    raw_payload: { synthetic: true },\n  });\n  const feed = [\n    event(\"evt_105\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:03.123456Z\", \"feed\"),\n    event(\"evt_104\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:02.123456Z\", \"feed\"),\n    event(\"evt_103\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:02.123456Z\", \"feed\"),\n    event(\"evt_102\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:02.123456Z\", \"feed\"),\n    event(\"evt_101\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:01.123456Z\", \"feed\"),\n  ];\n  const events = [\n    ...feed,\n    ...feed.slice(0, 4).map((item) =&gt; ({ ...item, project_id: \"exact\" })),\n    ...Array.from({ length: 105 }, (_, index) =&gt;\n      event(\n        `large_${String(index).padStart(3, \"0\")}`,\n        new Date(Date.UTC(2026, 0, 15, 12, 0, index))\n          .toISOString()\n          .replace(\".000Z\", \".123456Z\"),\n        \"large\"\n      )\n    ),\n    // Reverse ID order makes timestamp precision observable in the tests.\n    event(\"precise_a\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:00.123999Z\", \"precision\"),\n    event(\"precise_z\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:00.123001Z\", \"precision\"),\n    event(\"other_1\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:00.123456Z\", \"other\"),\n    event(\"other_2\", \"2026-01-15T11:59:59.123456Z\", \"other\"),\n    event(\"private_1\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:00.123456Z\", \"private\", \"tenant_b\"),\n    event(\"private_2\", \"2026-01-15T11:59:59.123456Z\", \"private\", \"tenant_b\"),\n  ];\n  return {\n    sessions,\n    projects,\n    events,\n    signingKey: randomBytes(32),\n    tokenA,\n    tokenB,\n  };\n}\n</code></pre> </details> <details> <summary>HTTP 契约和回归测试</summary> <pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">test(\"five-event traversal crosses a timestamp tie and replays the same continuation\", async () =&gt; {\n  const expected = [\"evt_105\", \"evt_104\", \"evt_103\", \"evt_102\", \"evt_101\"];\n  const pages = await traverse(\"feed\", 2, expected);\n  assert.deepEqual(pages.map(ids), [\n    [\"evt_105\", \"evt_104\"],\n    [\"evt_103\", \"evt_102\"],\n    [\"evt_101\"],\n  ]);\n  assert.equal(pages.length, 3);\n  assert.ok(pages[0].next_cursor);\n  assert.ok(pages[1].next_cursor);\n  assert.equal(pages[2].next_cursor, null);\n  const replay = await request(\"feed\", {\n    limit: \"2\",\n    cursor: pages[0].next_cursor,\n  });\n  assert.deepEqual(replay.body.items, pages[1].items);\n  const next = await request(\"feed\", {\n    limit: \"2\",\n    cursor: replay.body.next_cursor,\n  });\n  assert.deepEqual(next.body.items, pages[2].items);\n  assert.equal(next.body.next_cursor, null);\n  console.log(\n    JSON.stringify({\n      fixture: \"five-event-tie\",\n      pages: pages.map(ids),\n      requests: pages.length,\n      replay: ids(replay.body),\n    })\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"the same tie group traverses correctly with limit three\", async () =&gt; {\n  const pages = await traverse(\"feed\", 3, [\n    \"evt_105\",\n    \"evt_104\",\n    \"evt_103\",\n    \"evt_102\",\n    \"evt_101\",\n  ]);\n  assert.deepEqual(pages.map(ids), [\n    [\"evt_105\", \"evt_104\", \"evt_103\"],\n    [\"evt_102\", \"evt_101\"],\n  ]);\n});\n\ntest(\"timestamp ordering and continuation preserve submillisecond precision\", async () =&gt; {\n  const pages = await traverse(\"precision\", 1, [\"precise_a\", \"precise_z\"]);\n  assert.equal(pages[0].items[0].created_at, \"2026-01-15T12:00:00.123999Z\");\n  assert.equal(pages[1].items[0].created_at, \"2026-01-15T12:00:00.123001Z\");\n});\n\ntest(\"omitted, minimum, and maximum limits return 25, 1, and 100 of 105 events\", async () =&gt; {\n  for (const [parameters, expected] of [\n    [{}, 25],\n    [{ limit: \"1\" }, 1],\n    [{ limit: \"100\" }, 100],\n  ]) {\n    const result = await request(\"large\", parameters);\n    assert.equal(result.status, 200);\n    assert.equal(result.body.items.length, expected);\n    assert.ok(result.body.next_cursor);\n  }\n  const pages = await traverse(\n    \"large\",\n    100,\n    Array.from(\n      { length: 105 },\n      (_, index) =&gt; `large_${String(104 - index).padStart(3, \"0\")}`\n    )\n  );\n  assert.deepEqual(\n    pages.map((page) =&gt; page.items.length),\n    [100, 5]\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"invalid and repeated limits return the documented generic error\", async (context) =&gt; {\n  for (const limit of [\n    \"0\",\n    \"101\",\n    \"-1\",\n    \"1.5\",\n    \"many\",\n    \"\",\n    \"1e2\",\n    \"Infinity\",\n  ]) {\n    await context.test(`limit ${JSON.stringify(limit)}`, async () =&gt; {\n      const result = await request(\"feed\", { limit });\n      assert.equal(result.status, 400);\n      assert.deepEqual(\n        result.body,\n        expectedError(\n          \"invalid_limit\",\n          \"Limit must be an integer from 1 through 100.\"\n        )\n      );\n    });\n  }\n  const repeated = await request(\"feed\", [\n    [\"limit\", \"1\"],\n    [\"limit\", \"2\"],\n  ]);\n  assert.equal(repeated.status, 400);\n});\n\ntest(\"empty, partial, and exactly full final pages have no continuation\", async () =&gt; {\n  assert.deepEqual((await request(\"empty\")).body, {\n    items: [],\n    next_cursor: null,\n  });\n  const partial = await traverse(\"feed\", 2, [\n    \"evt_105\",\n    \"evt_104\",\n    \"evt_103\",\n    \"evt_102\",\n    \"evt_101\",\n  ]);\n  assert.equal(partial.at(-1).items.length, 1);\n  const exact = await traverse(\"exact\", 2, [\n    \"evt_105\",\n    \"evt_104\",\n    \"evt_103\",\n    \"evt_102\",\n  ]);\n  assert.deepEqual(\n    exact.map((page) =&gt; page.items.length),\n    [2, 2]\n  );\n  assert.equal(exact[1].next_cursor, null);\n});\n\ntest(\"authentication precedes malformed and wrong-scope cursor or limit validation\", async () =&gt; {\n  const privateCursor = (\n    await request(\"private\", { limit: \"1\" }, fixtures.tokenB)\n  ).body.next_cursor;\n  for (const token of [null, \"invalid_session\"]) {\n    for (const parameters of [\n      { cursor: \"broken\" },\n      { cursor: privateCursor },\n      { limit: \"0\", cursor: \"broken\" },\n    ]) {\n      const result = await request(\"feed\", parameters, token);\n      assert.equal(result.status, 401);\n      assert.deepEqual(result.body, unauthenticated);\n    }\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"inaccessible and nonexistent projects return identical 404 before cursor validation\", async () =&gt; {\n  const ownCursor = (await request(\"feed\", { limit: \"1\" })).body.next_cursor;\n  for (const project of [\"private\", \"missing\"]) {\n    for (const parameters of [\n      {},\n      { cursor: \"broken\" },\n      { cursor: ownCursor },\n      { limit: \"0\", cursor: \"broken\" },\n    ]) {\n      const result = await request(project, parameters);\n      assert.equal(result.status, 404);\n      assert.deepEqual(result.body, notFound);\n    }\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"a valid cursor from another project in the same tenant is invalid on an authorized feed\", async () =&gt; {\n  const cursor = (await request(\"other\", { limit: \"1\" })).body.next_cursor;\n  assert.ok(cursor);\n  const result = await request(\"feed\", { cursor });\n  assert.equal(result.status, 400);\n  assert.deepEqual(result.body, invalidCursor);\n});\n\ntest(\"a valid cursor from another tenant is invalid on an authorized feed\", async () =&gt; {\n  const cursor = (await request(\"private\", { limit: \"1\" }, fixtures.tokenB))\n    .body.next_cursor;\n  assert.ok(cursor);\n  const result = await request(\"feed\", { cursor });\n  assert.equal(result.status, 400);\n  assert.deepEqual(result.body, invalidCursor);\n});\n\ntest(\"undecodable, empty, tampered, and repeated cursor tokens return the same closed error\", async () =&gt; {\n  const cursor = (await request(\"feed\", { limit: \"1\" })).body.next_cursor;\n  const [payload, signature] = cursor.split(\".\");\n  const tampered = `${payload}.${signature[0] === \"A\" ? \"B\" : \"A\"}${signature.slice(1)}`;\n  for (const token of [\n    \"broken\",\n    \"\",\n    \"%%%.___\",\n    \"a.b.c\",\n    \"x\".repeat(2049),\n    tampered,\n  ]) {\n    const result = await request(\"feed\", { cursor: token });\n    assert.equal(result.status, 400);\n    assert.deepEqual(result.body, invalidCursor);\n  }\n  const result = await request(\"feed\", [\n    [\"cursor\", cursor],\n    [\"cursor\", cursor],\n  ]);\n  assert.equal(result.status, 400);\n  assert.deepEqual(result.body, invalidCursor);\n});\n\ntest(\"signed structurally invalid payloads and unsupported versions are rejected\", async (context) =&gt; {\n  const valid = {\n    version: 1,\n    tenant_id: \"tenant_a\",\n    project_id: \"feed\",\n    created_at: \"2026-01-15T12:00:02.123456Z\",\n    id: \"evt_104\",\n  };\n  const missing = { ...valid };\n  delete missing.id;\n  const cases = [\n    [\"missing ID\", missing],\n    [\"number ID\", { ...valid, id: 104 }],\n    [\"empty ID\", { ...valid, id: \"\" }],\n    [\"number timestamp\", { ...valid, created_at: 0 }],\n    [\"invalid date\", { ...valid, created_at: \"2026-02-30T12:00:00Z\" }],\n    [\"unsupported version\", { ...valid, version: 2 }],\n    [\"extra field\", { ...valid, extra: true }],\n    [\"wrong tenant type\", { ...valid, tenant_id: 1 }],\n    [\"wrong project type\", { ...valid, project_id: null }],\n    [\"null payload\", null],\n    [\"array payload\", []],\n    [\"invalid JSON\", \"not-json\"],\n  ];\n  for (const [name, payload] of cases) {\n    await context.test(name, async () =&gt; {\n      const result = await request(\"feed\", { cursor: signFixture(payload) });\n      assert.equal(result.status, 400);\n      assert.deepEqual(result.body, invalidCursor);\n    });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"every serialized event omits stored tenant, project, and raw payload fields\", async () =&gt; {\n  const result = await request(\"feed\", { limit: \"100\" });\n  assert.equal(result.status, 200);\n  for (const item of result.body.items) {\n    assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(item).sort(), [\n      \"created_at\",\n      \"id\",\n      \"summary\",\n      \"type\",\n    ]);\n  }\n  assert.ok(\n    fixtures.events.some((event) =&gt; event.internal_note &amp;&amp; event.raw_payload)\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"the schema oracle rejects extra, missing, incorrectly typed, and malformed public fields\", () =&gt; {\n  const schema = specification.components.schemas.EventPage;\n  const page = {\n    items: [\n      {\n        id: \"evt_1\",\n        created_at: \"2026-01-15T12:00:00.123456Z\",\n        type: \"deployment\",\n        summary: \"Synthetic\",\n      },\n    ],\n    next_cursor: null,\n  };\n  assert.ok(conforms(page, schema));\n  assert.equal(conforms({ ...page, tenant_id: \"tenant_a\" }, schema), false);\n  assert.equal(\n    conforms(\n      { ...page, items: [{ ...page.items[0], raw_payload: {} }] },\n      schema\n    ),\n    false\n  );\n  assert.equal(conforms({ items: page.items }, schema), false);\n  assert.equal(conforms({ ...page, next_cursor: \"\" }, schema), false);\n  assert.equal(\n    conforms({ ...page, items: [{ ...page.items[0], id: 1 }] }, schema),\n    false\n  );\n  assert.equal(\n    conforms(\n      { ...page, items: [{ ...page.items[0], created_at: \"yesterday\" }] },\n      schema\n    ),\n    false\n  );\n  const errorSchema = specification.components.schemas.InvalidCursor;\n  assert.equal(\n    conforms(\n      { error: { ...invalidCursor.error, stack: \"internal\" } },\n      errorSchema\n    ),\n    false\n  );\n  assert.equal(\n    conforms(\n      { error: { ...invalidCursor.error, message: \"tenant_a\" } },\n      errorSchema\n    ),\n    false\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"the existing project-detail route preserves access and ignores pagination parameters\", async () =&gt; {\n  const own = await request(\n    \"feed\",\n    { cursor: \"broken\", limit: \"0\" },\n    fixtures.tokenA,\n    true\n  );\n  assert.equal(own.status, 200);\n  assert.deepEqual(own.body, { id: \"feed\", name: \"Activity feed\" });\n  const inaccessible = await request(\"private\", {}, fixtures.tokenA, true);\n  assert.equal(inaccessible.status, 404);\n  assert.deepEqual(inaccessible.body, notFound);\n  const unauthenticatedResult = await request(\"feed\", {}, null, true);\n  assert.equal(unauthenticatedResult.status, 401);\n  assert.deepEqual(unauthenticatedResult.body, unauthenticated);\n});\n\ntest(\"OpenAPI declares operation, limit boundaries, signed cursor, and response statuses\", () =&gt; {\n  assert.equal(specification.openapi, \"3.1.0\");\n  const operation = specification.paths[\"/v1/projects/{project_id}/events\"].get;\n  assert.equal(operation.operationId, \"listProjectEvents\");\n  const limit = operation.parameters.find(\n    (parameter) =&gt; parameter.name === \"limit\"\n  ).schema;\n  assert.deepEqual(limit, {\n    type: \"integer\",\n    minimum: 1,\n    maximum: 100,\n    default: 25,\n  });\n  assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(operation.responses).sort(), [\n    \"200\",\n    \"400\",\n    \"401\",\n    \"404\",\n  ]);\n  assert.equal(\n    specification.components.securitySchemes.session.scheme,\n    \"bearer\"\n  );\n});\n</code></pre> </details> <details> <summary>证据采集</summary> <pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">mkdirSync(output, { recursive: true });\nconst states = [];\nfor (const [name, arguments_] of [\n  [\"red\", [\"--seeded\"]],\n  [\"green\", []],\n]) {\n  const result = spawnSync(\n    process.execPath,\n    [resolve(directory, \"test.mjs\"), ...arguments_],\n    {\n      cwd: directory,\n      encoding: \"utf8\",\n      timeout: 30_000,\n    }\n  );\n  writeFileSync(\n    resolve(output, `${name}.log`),\n    `${result.stdout ?? \"\"}${result.stderr ?? \"\"}`\n  );\n  states.push({\n    name,\n    command: `node test.mjs${arguments_.length ? \" --seeded\" : \"\"}`,\n    exit_code: result.status,\n    signal: result.signal,\n    error: result.error?.message ?? null,\n  });\n}\nconst sources = Object.fromEntries(\n  readdirSync(directory, { withFileTypes: true })\n    .filter((entry) =&gt; entry.isFile())\n    .map((entry) =&gt; [\n      entry.name,\n      createHash(\"sha256\")\n        .update(readFileSync(resolve(directory, entry.name)))\n        .digest(\"hex\"),\n    ])\n);\nconst observed = { red: await observe(true), green: await observe(false) };\nwriteJson(\"observed-http.json\", observed);\nwriteJson(\"run-manifest.json\", {\n  execution: \"Synthetic loopback HTTP fixture; no external service\",\n  recorded_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n  node: process.version,\n  minimum_node: \"22.6.0\",\n  dependencies: \"Node standard library only; no install step\",\n  baseline:\n    \"Deliberately seeded timestamp-only continuation; not a historical customer defect\",\n  correction:\n    \"Descending timestamp-and-ID tuple continuation using full fractional precision\",\n  source_sha256: sources,\n  states,\n});\nif (\n  states[0].exit_code === null ||\n  states[0].exit_code === 0 ||\n  states[1].exit_code !== 0\n) {\n  throw new Error(\n    \"Expected the unchanged tests to fail on the seeded baseline and pass on the corrected implementation. Inspect red.log and green.log.\"\n  );\n}\nconsole.log(\n  JSON.stringify(\n    {\n      execution: \"synthetic-loopback-http\",\n      red_exit: states[0].exit_code,\n      green_exit: states[1].exit_code,\n      green_pages: observed.green.pages.map((page) =&gt;\n        page.body.items.map((item) =&gt; item.id)\n      ),\n      evidence_directory: output,\n    },\n    null,\n    2\n  )\n);\n</code></pre> </details> <p><a id=\"prepare-the-input-packet\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">准备输入资料包</h2> <p>只有当 Codex 能够读取问题单内容时，问题单链接才有用。如果无法访问来源，请直接粘贴或附上相关内容。使用起始提示词时，请包含以下信息。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>输入</th> <th>示例问题单</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>问题单和预期结果</td> <td><code>API-142</code>：新增 <code>GET /v1/projects/{project_id}/events</code>，让客户可以分页查看活动动态。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>代码库和基线</td> <td>将示例文件夹放入你选择的代码库，然后记录任务所选的分支和确切提交。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>相关代码</td> <td>示例中的 <code>api.mjs</code>、<code>fixtures.mjs</code>、<code>test.mjs</code> 和 <code>openapi.json</code>，以及你代码库中的 <code>AGENTS.md</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>现有模式</td> <td>保持分页验证之前的身份验证和项目授权。使用签名游标和文档规定的公开错误封装。改编问题单时，遵循代码库现有辅助函数的模式。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>测试设置</td> <td>为两个租户准备固定的内存测试项目，其中租户 A 有六个项目；设置一个跨越分页边界的时间戳并列组、具有小数精度的时间戳、空的及正好填满的末页，以及 105 个事件用于检查上限。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>验证</td> <td><code>node test.mjs --seeded</code>（预期失败）、<code>node test.mjs</code>（修正后的状态）以及 <code>node reproduce.mjs ./evidence</code>。对每个 <code>.mjs</code> 文件运行 <code>node --check</code>。对于你自己的服务，请补充实际使用的类型、lint、回归和 CI 命令。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>范围</td> <td>端点、聚焦测试及其 OpenAPI 文档。不添加新依赖、不迁移数据库、不做前端改动、不部署，也不重新设计身份验证。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>交接</td> <td>如果已有代码库集成支持且你已授权创建，则创建草稿 PR；否则提供差异和草稿 PR 说明。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>对于示例，请准备 Node 22.6 或更高版本；测试会自行创建测试会话和游标签名密钥，并将临时 HTTP 服务器绑定到本机回环接口。对于你自己的服务，还要准备其依赖项、测试配置和隔离服务。分配此问题单之前，应确认现有游标辅助函数能够将游标绑定到已认证的租户和请求的项目。</p> <p><a id=\"define-the-api-contract\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"api\">定义 API 契约</h3> <p>实施之前，应先确认下述示例契约与你的代码库相符。成功响应为 HTTP 200，且字段只能包含 <code>{ items, next_cursor }</code>。</p> <p>每个 item 恰好有四个必需公开字段：<code>id</code>（非空字符串）、<code>created_at</code>（UTC RFC 3339 时间戳字符串）、<code>type</code>（非空字符串）和 <code>summary</code>（字符串）。<code>items</code> 是这些对象组成的数组；<code>next_cursor</code> 是不透明的非空字符串或 <code>null</code>。</p> <p>内部租户/项目键、数据库元数据、原始事件载荷和凭据都不是响应字段。应在 OpenAPI 中说明响应字段类型、必需字段、字段是否允许为 <code>null</code>，以及封闭的对象结构。请根据该模式验证序列化后的 HTTP 正文。</p> <p>事件按照 <code>created_at DESC, id DESC</code> 排序，保留时间戳的小数精度，并按 ID 的字典序降序排列。游标应按照该顺序，从最后一个已返回的元组之后继续。</p> <p>默认每页数量为 25；有效 limit 是从 1 到 100 的十进制整数。重复出现的 limit 或游标参数无效。只有在还存在其他匹配事件时，才返回非空游标。</p> <p>无论最后一页只包含部分结果还是正好填满，<code>next_cursor: null</code> 都应作为游标值；已授权项目中没有事件时，返回 <code>items: []</code> 和 <code>next_cursor: null</code>。</p> <p>示例会对每个游标签名，并将其绑定到已认证的租户和请求的项目。验证 limit 或游标之前，先对请求项目进行身份验证和授权，这样参数错误就不会泄露其他租户的项目是否存在。</p> <p>缺失或无效会话返回 401；无权访问或不存在的项目都返回相同的通用 404。确认有访问权限后，先检查 limit，再检查游标。</p> <p>格式错误、遭到篡改、结构无效，或与租户/项目不匹配的游标应返回 HTTP 400，错误码为 <code>invalid_cursor</code>。同一租户中属于另一项目的有效游标，以及在另一租户下签发的有效游标，在当前已授权项目中使用时都属于无效游标。</p> <p>提供的游标不得改变对无权访问项目的授权结果。示例中的第 1 版游标不会过期；不支持的版本属于无效游标。</p> <p>示例中的每个错误正文都只能包含 <code>{ error: { code, message } }</code>，且两个字段都必须是必需的字符串，不得包含其他字段。</p> <p>使用以下通用错误响应：</p> <ul> <li>400 <code>invalid_cursor</code> / <code>Invalid cursor.</code></li> <li>400 <code>invalid_limit</code> / <code>Limit must be an integer from 1 through 100.</code></li> <li>401 <code>unauthenticated</code> / <code>Authentication required.</code></li> <li>404 <code>not_found</code> / <code>Project not found.</code></li> </ul> <p>所有错误正文中都不得包含解码后的游标内容、租户/项目标识符、原始错误或堆栈跟踪。如果真实代码库采用不同的获准错误封装或错误码，应使用实际规则；若契约不同，在更改共享辅助函数之前先解决差异。</p> <p>遍历和重放断言使用没有并发写入的固定夹具：连续使用游标应按约定顺序恰好返回每个事件一次，并且对于非空动态列表，请求次数不超过 <code>ceil(event_count / limit)</code>；对于空列表，请求一次即可。</p> <p>只要夹具保持不变，使用相同请求参数重放有效游标，就应返回相同项目和后续位置；签名 Token 不要求逐字节完全相同。</p> <p>此契约不保证游标只能使用一次、不保证快照分页，也不保证动态列表变化后结果仍相同。请记录代码库现有的动态列表一致性策略；如果没有策略且问题单要求快照行为，请停止并请求产品决定。</p> <p><a id=\"how-to-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">使用方法</h2> <ol> <li><strong>选择问题单并准备环境。</strong> 确认上述契约符合实际代码库。选择准备好的云端环境和目标基线提交。直接在任务中提供问题单资料包；开始此流程不依赖自动的问题跟踪器触发。</li> <li><strong>运行起始提示词。</strong> 将方括号输入替换为代码库、问题单资料包、边界和检查项。选择让 Codex 返回差异，还是创建已获授权的草稿 PR。本页的起始提示词包含完整的交接要求。</li> <li><strong>建立基线。</strong> Codex 应先阅读代码库指引，并在编辑之前运行获准的基线检查。</li> </ol> <p>示例应运行 <code>node test.mjs</code> 和 <code>README.md</code> 中的语法检查；<code>--seeded</code> 是单独演示故意失败的命令。</p> <p>对于你自己的服务，应运行现有回归、类型和 lint 检查。新端点的聚焦测试文件可能尚不存在；请将其记录为待创建测试。将既有检查失败或测试服务不可用的问题先处理好，再判断后续结果是否由新功能引起。</p> <ol> <li><strong>实现并验证契约。</strong> 要求 Codex 使用现有访问权限和游标辅助函数来实现端点、添加下列验收测试，并更新 API 文档。在可行的情况下，新测试应先在原始代码上失败，再在更改后通过。请将测试结果与最终验证记录一起保存。可下载示例使用 <code>--seeded</code> 选择一个预置缺陷进行对比；这与代码库基线中原本存在的失败是两回事。</li> <li><strong>审核更改及其证据。</strong> 一起阅读差异、验收检查、检查输出和剩余风险。如果 Codex 创建了已获授权的草稿 PR，请核实其 base 和 head 是否正确。如果 PR 工具不可用，就使用返回的差异和说明，按常规流程准备 PR。请在草稿 PR 中列出未解决的检查，并保持其不可合并状态。</li> <li><strong>处理审核反馈并按常规流程合并。</strong> 在同一任务中向 Codex 提供需要处理的具体评论，然后重新运行受影响的检查。审核者应在最终提交合并之前确认所需 CI 通过并批准变更。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"acceptance-tests-to-require\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">应要求添加的验收测试</h2> <p>这些测试让问题单保持足够小，便于分派和审核。可根据测试运行器调整测试名称，但必须保留每项测试要验证的行为。</p> <p><a id=\"stable-traversal\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_11\">稳定遍历</h3> <p>植入五个固定事件：<code>evt_105</code> 的时间戳最新；<code>evt_104</code>、<code>evt_103</code> 和 <code>evt_102</code> 的时间戳相同且居中；<code>evt_101</code> 的时间戳最旧。</p> <p>使用 <code>limit=2</code> 时，要求恰好返回以下页面：<code>[evt_105, evt_104]</code>、<code>[evt_103, evt_102]</code>、<code>[evt_101]</code>。同一时间戳的事件组必须跨越第一页边界。</p> <p>断言顺序准确、没有重复或缺失 ID、前两页游标非空、第三页游标为 null；如果遍历超过三次请求则测试失败。</p> <p>在夹具未变化时，使用相同的 limit 重放第一页返回的后续游标，并断言第二页项目和后续位置相同。</p> <p><a id=\"default-and-boundary-sizes\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_12\">默认和边界数量</h3> <p>植入超过 100 个事件。断言未提供 <code>limit</code> 时返回 25 条，<code>limit=1</code> 时返回一条，<code>limit=100</code> 时返回 100 条。</p> <p><a id=\"invalid-limits\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_13\">无效的数量限制</h3> <p>使用现有验证错误形状，断言 <code>0</code>、<code>101</code>、<code>-1</code>、小数值和 <code>many</code> 等字符串都会返回 HTTP 400。</p> <p><a id=\"empty-and-final-pages\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_14\">空页面和最后一页</h3> <p>断言已授权项目为空时返回 <code>items: []</code> 和 <code>next_cursor: null</code>。当 <code>limit=2</code> 时，五个事件应在第三页返回一条且游标为 null；四个事件应在第二页返回两条且游标为 null。最后一页已填满时，不应再额外请求一个空页面。</p> <p><a id=\"authentication\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_15\">身份验证</h3> <p>断言缺失或无效会话会返回约定的 401 模式，包括携带格式错误游标或其他范围游标的请求。游标验证不得覆盖身份验证结果。</p> <p><a id=\"tenant-isolation\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_16\">租户隔离</h3> <p>使用租户 A 的身份请求租户 B 的项目或不存在的项目。断言返回相同的通用 404 正文，且不包含事件数据；即使请求携带格式错误或范围不匹配的游标，也应如此。授权检查必须先于游标验证。</p> <p><a id=\"cursor-scope\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_17\">游标范围</h3> <p>请求租户 A 中有权访问的项目，并分别提供：（1）来自该租户另一个项目的有效签名游标；（2）在租户 B 下签发的有效签名游标。</p> <p>断言两者都返回相同的 HTTP 400 <code>invalid_cursor</code> 正文，不包含事件数据或范围细节。应将这两类测试与请求无权访问项目的情况分开；后者必须返回 404。</p> <p><a id=\"malformed-and-tampered-cursors\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_18\">格式错误或遭篡改的游标</h3> <p>在已授权项目上，断言游标辅助函数无法解码的 Token、签名已被修改的 Token，以及缺少必需游标字段或字段类型错误的已签名 Token，都会返回 HTTP 400 <code>invalid_cursor</code>。使用隔离的测试签名夹具。</p> <p>如果共享辅助函数支持不受支持的版本或过期 Token，也应覆盖这些情况。断言响应符合约定的通用错误模式，并且不包含解码内容、标识符、原始错误或堆栈跟踪。</p> <p><a id=\"existing-behavior\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_19\">既有行为</h3> <p>示例会通过已授权、未授权和项目不可访问的请求检查现有项目详情路由。运行其 <code>.mjs</code> 文件的语法检查。在自己的服务中，运行既定回归套件、类型检查和 lint。</p> <p><a id=\"public-response-schema\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_20\">公开响应模式</h3> <p>根据约定的 OpenAPI 模式验证实际 HTTP 200、400、401 和 404 正文。断言必需键、item 字段类型、时间戳格式、游标是否允许 <code>null</code>，以及所有层级的对象都没有额外属性。</p> <p>在存储的事件中植入内部字段，并确认序列化后的项目中不会泄露这些字段；同时确认每个错误响应只包含获准的通用错误码和消息。</p> <p><a id=\"documentation\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_21\">文档</h3> <p>确认 OpenAPI 操作和示例与已实现的参数、准确的成功/错误模式、授权优先顺序、排序方式、最后一页规则，以及固定夹具下重放/一致性的限制相符。如果代码库提供 API 规范验证工具，也要运行它。</p> <p><a id=\"what-good-output-looks-like\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_22\">良好输出的样子</h2> <p><a id=\"shared-evidence-record\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_23\">共享证据记录</h3> <p>对每项验收标准使用以下证据格式，并根据实际输出填写。如果基线中尚不存在新测试，应将“尚未添加”与现有检查失败区分开来。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Criterion / test: [specific behavior and test location]\nEnvironment: [published setup reference; runtime, database and dependency versions]\nBefore: [revision + test-only diff ID; command; exit code; observed assertion; log path]\nAfter: [final revision or base + diff ID; command; exit code; observed assertion; log path]\nStatus: [pass / fail / blocked / not run]\nLimits / reviewer action: [untested behavior, blocker, or decision required]\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>模板中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">验收标准 / 测试：[specific behavior and test location]\n环境：[published setup reference; runtime, database and dependency versions]\n修改前：[revision + test-only diff ID; command; exit code; observed assertion; log path]\n修改后：[final revision or base + diff ID; command; exit code; observed assertion; log path]\n状态：[pass / fail / blocked / not run]\n局限 / 审阅者需处理的事项：[untested behavior, blocker, or decision required]</div></div> <p>红灯和绿灯运行都应绑定到实际测试过的状态，包括在原始修订上添加的仅供测试的更改。交接材料中应保存日志、响应夹具和最终差异；只有文件名和测试名不能证明测试实际运行过。受测修订发生变化时，应更新证据。受阻或尚未运行的检查不能算作通过。</p> <p>有用的 PR 说明会为每项声明链接相应证据。请使用以下交接模板，并将所有方括号字段替换为实际观察结果。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Title: Add cursor pagination for project events\nIssue: API-142\nBase: [branch and commit]\nTested state: [head commit, or base commit plus attached diff identifier]\n\nChanges\n- Add the project-events endpoint using the existing project access helper.\n- Reuse signed cursors scoped to tenant and project.\n- Add contract tests and update the OpenAPI operation.\n\nAcceptance evidence\n- [One row per criterion above: test, observed result, and log reference.]\n\nValidation\n- Before edits: [command, result, and log reference for each baseline check].\n- New tests against original code: [result, or not run with reason].\n- After edits: [command, result, and log reference for each required check].\n- CI: [check links and actual states, or not available].\n- Remaining checks: [specific checks and blockers, or none with supporting evidence].\n\nReviewer focus\n- [Highest-risk behavior and unresolved criteria.]\n\nRemaining risk and rollback\n- [Observed limitations; distinguish them from untested assumptions.]\n- [How this change can be reverted and whether any callers depend on it.]\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>模板中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">标题：为项目事件添加游标分页\n问题：API-142\n基线：[branch and commit]\n受测状态：[head commit, or base commit plus attached diff identifier]\n\n变更\n- 使用现有的项目访问检查辅助函数，添加项目事件端点。\n- 复用限定到租户和项目范围的签名游标。\n- 添加契约测试，并更新 OpenAPI 操作。\n\n验收证据\n- [One row per criterion above: test, observed result, and log reference.]\n\n验证\n- 修改前：[command, result, and log reference for each baseline check].\n- 在原始代码上运行新测试：[result, or not run with reason].\n- 修改后：[command, result, and log reference for each required check].\n- CI：[check links and actual states, or not available].\n- 剩余检查：[specific checks and blockers, or none with supporting evidence].\n\n审阅重点\n- [Highest-risk behavior and unresolved criteria.]\n\n剩余风险与回滚\n- [Observed limitations; distinguish them from untested assumptions.]\n- [How this change can be reverted and whether any callers depend on it.]</div></div> <p><a id=\"iterate-from-review-comments\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_24\">根据审核评论继续迭代</h2> <p>针对具体审核问题使用聚焦的后续提示。例如：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Address this review comment in the current change:\n\"Repeat the five-event traversal with limit=3; assert pages\n[evt_105, evt_104, evt_103] and [evt_102, evt_101], then a null cursor.\"\n\nAdd the regression test and change the implementation only if it exposes a\nfailure. Rerun the focused endpoint tests and any other required checks affected\nby the edit. Update the evidence table with the tested state and actual results.\nKeep the same scope. Do not merge or deploy.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">处理当前更改中的这条审查意见：\n“以 limit=3 重复遍历这五个事件；断言分页结果为\n[evt_105, evt_104, evt_103] 和 [evt_102, evt_101]，然后游标为 null。”\n\n添加回归测试；只有测试暴露出失败时，才修改实现。\n重新运行聚焦的端点测试，以及受此次修改影响的其他必要检查。\n在证据表中更新接受测试的状态和实际结果。\n保持相同范围。不要合并或部署。</div></div> <p>如果 Codex 无法直接查看审核内容，请提供评论文本。审核者应检查回复是否真正解决了相关行为问题，而不是只满足评论措辞。</p> <p><a id=\"when-to-stop\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_25\">何时停止</h2> <ul> <li><strong>基线失败或无法运行。</strong> 返回失败的检查和环境设置详情。继续之前，应修复环境或商定并记录基线。</li> <li><strong>契约与现有行为冲突。</strong> 指出冲突、受影响的调用方和所需的最小决定。不要悄悄改变契约。</li> <li><strong>更改需要迁移、新依赖或重新设计身份验证。</strong> 说明原因，并在扩大范围之前拆分任务或重新界定范围。</li> <li><strong>实现后测试失败。</strong> 不要将更改标记为可合并。报告失败的用例。不要删除断言或弱化授权要求来让测试通过。</li> <li><strong>无法使用代码库写入集成。</strong> 返回差异、草稿 PR 说明和验证证据。队友可以按代码库常规流程完成交接。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"reuse-the-workflow\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_26\">复用此工作流</h2> <p>审核者接受第一个结果之后，可将问题资料包和验收清单保存到团队的问题单模板中。将稳定的代码库指引（例如测试命令和 API 契约所在位置）记录在 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 或现有贡献者指南中。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"turn-an-issue-into-a-tested-pull-request\">Turn an issue into a tested pull request</h1> <p>Hand off a small feature with acceptance criteria and review the evidence.</p> <p>Give Codex a scoped issue, a prepared cloud environment, and explicit checks. Get an implementation, tests, documentation, and a reviewable change with evidence for each acceptance criterion.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Startup engineers implementing a scoped API issue.</li> <li>Reviewers who need implementation and validation evidence together.</li> <li>Teams with acceptance criteria and a working test environment.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Implement a scoped issue</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Implement [issue ID and title] in [repository] at [base branch and commit],\nusing the prepared cloud environment I selected for this task.\n\nInput packet: [paste or attach the issue, acceptance criteria, relevant\nfiles, public success/error schemas, authorization and pagination contract,\ntest fixtures, and approved validation commands].\nRepository instructions: [AGENTS.md and any relevant nested instructions].\nScope: [files or component boundaries].\nOut of scope: [explicit exclusions].\nRequired checks: [focused tests, relevant regression tests, type check,\nlint, and any required CI checks].\nOutput: [create a draft PR in this repository if the available integration\nsupports it and I authorize it here / return a diff and draft PR description].\n\nFirst read the instructions and relevant code. Confirm the starting commit\nand run the existing baseline checks using the execution tools available\nin this environment. Record any new test files as still to be created.\nIf the baseline fails, access is missing, or a\nrequired check cannot run, report the exact blocker before implementing.\n\nState a short plan, then implement the smallest change that meets the\nacceptance criteria. Follow existing auth, error, pagination, and testing\npatterns. Add tests that distinguish the required behavior from the old\nbehavior. For this pagination example, require tied timestamps across a\npage boundary, bounded traversal and replay on fixed fixtures, partial and\nexact-full final pages, authorization before cursor validation, invalid\ncursor cases, and success/error schema checks. Update the affected API\ndocumentation to match the implemented public response exactly.\n\nAfter implementation, run the required checks again. For every acceptance\ncriterion, point to the test or other evidence that verifies it. Record\ncommands, results, the tested commit or working-tree state, and any checks\nthat were not run. Separate pre-existing failures from new failures.\nNever describe an unrun check as passing.\n\nDeliver the diff or authorized draft PR, a concise change summary, the\nacceptance-criteria evidence table, remaining risks, and reviewer actions.\nDo not merge, deploy, use production data, change permissions, add new\ndependencies, or expand the agreed scope. Stop for a decision if the\ncontract conflicts with the repository or the work needs a schema change.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/issue-to-tested-pr/sample.zip\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Download the runnable sample (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">Cloud environments</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9563acffd5862bcd\">Keep documentation up-to-date</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Hand Codex a small, well-defined issue and ask for a change a teammate can review: implementation, tests, documentation, and evidence that the requested behavior works. Keep the task in one prepared cloud environment so the code and validation use the same repository setup.</p> <ol> <li> <p>In the web or desktop app, choose <strong>Work in</strong> &gt; <strong>Cloud</strong> and select a published environment.</p> </li> <li> <p>To create one, select <strong>Create environment</strong>, choose the GitHub repositories, and ask Codex to prepare the runtime, dependencies, and isolated test services.</p> </li> <li> <p>Review the setup report, resolve failed checks, and <strong>Publish</strong> before starting a new task.</p> </li> <li> <p>Follow the <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">current Cloud environment guide</a>.</p> </li> <li>Keep repository guidance in <a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">AGENTS.md</a>.</li> </ol> <p>If dependencies change or service setup changes, edit the reusable environment, test it, and <strong>Republish</strong>, then verify the changes in a new task.</p> <p>Repository refresh does not rerun install/start commands, and existing tasks keep their own state.</p> <p>Configure required network destinations and test credentials separately; allowing a destination does not grant service access.</p> <p>If required checks cannot run, finish setup before using this workflow.</p> <h2 id=\"when-to-use-it\">When to use it</h2> <p>Choose a feature with a written contract and a clear stopping point: a new API endpoint, a validation rule, or a small addition to an existing service. The issue should fit in one pull request and have checks that can run without production access.</p> <p>The example adds pagination to a project's activity feed. The runnable Node.js sample includes authentication, project access, signed cursors, and an existing project-detail route. It uses fixed test records in memory, so you can check the pagination contract without a database or external service.</p> <h2 id=\"try-the-runnable-sample\">Try the runnable sample</h2> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/issue-to-tested-pr/sample.zip\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Download the sample (online)</a>, extract it, and open its <code>issue-to-tested-pr</code> folder. Use <strong>Node 22.6 or later</strong>. The sample uses the standard library and needs no package installation or API key.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">node --version\nnode api.mjs\nnode test.mjs --seeded\nnode test.mjs\nnode reproduce.mjs ./evidence\n</code></pre> <p><code>node api.mjs</code> starts a local HTTP server, requests the first page, prints its public IDs, and closes the server.</p> <p>The <code>--seeded</code> test run deliberately exits nonzero: its timestamp-only continuation skips two events tied at the first page boundary. The same tests pass with the corrected timestamp-and-ID tuple continuation.</p> <p>The reproduction command succeeds only if the seeded state fails and the corrected state passes.</p> <p>The corrected traversal with <code>limit=2</code> returns these pages in three requests:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">[evt_105, evt_104]\n[evt_103, evt_102]\n[evt_101]\n</code></pre> <p>The first two pages have a continuation cursor; the final page has <code>next_cursor: null</code>.</p> <p>The seeded state returns <code>[evt_105, evt_104]</code>, then <code>[evt_101]</code>, losing <code>evt_103</code> and <code>evt_102</code>.</p> <p>A successful run passes all 36 tests in the corrected state. The seeded state fails three assertions that expose the pagination defect.</p> <p>To verify your environment, put the files in your selected repository, prepare and publish an environment with a supported Node runtime, then run the commands in a new Cloud task and record its results.</p> <p><code>reproduce.mjs</code> saves <code>red.log</code>, <code>green.log</code>, <code>observed-http.json</code>, and <code>run-manifest.json</code> in the requested evidence directory. The manifest identifies the runtime, commands, exit codes, seeded defect, correction, and SHA-256 source hashes.</p> <p>It does not record session tokens or the signing key. Read <code>README.md</code> and <code>openapi.json</code> for the sample's setup and public contract.</p> <h3 id=\"inspect-the-runnable-sample\">Inspect the runnable sample</h3> <p>These excerpts come from the files in the download. Run the complete files after extracting the ZIP.</p> <details> <summary>Cursor and ordering implementation</summary> <pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">export function createApi({\n  sessions,\n  projects,\n  events,\n  signingKey,\n  seededBug = false,\n}) {\n  return createServer((request, response) =&gt; {\n    const send = (status, body) =&gt; {\n      response.writeHead(status, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n      response.end(JSON.stringify(body));\n    };\n    const fail = (code) =&gt; {\n      const [status, message] = errors[code];\n      send(status, { error: { code, message } });\n    };\n    // Authenticate, then authorize. Malformed parameters must not change these results.\n    const authorization = request.headers.authorization ?? \"\";\n    const bearer = /^Bearer ([A-Za-z0-9_-]+)$/.exec(authorization);\n    const tenantId = bearer ? sessions.get(bearer[1]) : undefined;\n    if (!tenantId) return fail(\"unauthenticated\");\n\n    const url = new URL(request.url ?? \"/\", \"http://127.0.0.1\");\n    const route = /^\\/v1\\/projects\\/([^/]+)(\\/events)?$/.exec(url.pathname);\n    let projectId;\n    try {\n      projectId = route ? decodeURIComponent(route[1]) : undefined;\n    } catch {\n      return fail(\"not_found\");\n    }\n    const project = projectId ? projects.get(projectId) : undefined;\n    if (\n      request.method !== \"GET\" ||\n      !project ||\n      project.tenant_id !== tenantId\n    ) {\n      return fail(\"not_found\");\n    }\n    // Existing project-detail behavior remains independent of pagination parameters.\n    if (!route[2]) return send(200, { id: projectId, name: project.name });\n\n    const rawLimit = url.searchParams.get(\"limit\");\n    const limit = rawLimit === null ? 25 : Number(rawLimit);\n    if (\n      url.searchParams.getAll(\"limit\").length &gt; 1 ||\n      (rawLimit !== null &amp;&amp; !/^\\d+$/.test(rawLimit)) ||\n      !Number.isInteger(limit) ||\n      limit &lt; 1 ||\n      limit &gt; 100\n    ) {\n      return fail(\"invalid_limit\");\n    }\n    let cursor;\n    if (url.searchParams.has(\"cursor\")) {\n      try {\n        if (url.searchParams.getAll(\"cursor\").length !== 1)\n          throw new Error(\"Invalid cursor\");\n        cursor = decodeCursor(\n          url.searchParams.get(\"cursor\"),\n          tenantId,\n          projectId,\n          signingKey\n        );\n      } catch {\n        return fail(\"invalid_cursor\");\n      }\n    }\n\n    const matching = events\n      .filter(\n        (event) =&gt;\n          event.tenant_id === tenantId &amp;&amp; event.project_id === projectId\n      )\n      .sort(compareEvents)\n      .filter((event) =&gt; {\n        if (!cursor) return true;\n        // Deliberate baseline defect: timestamp-only continuation loses tied rows.\n        if (seededBug)\n          return (\n            timestampValue(event.created_at) &lt; timestampValue(cursor.created_at)\n          );\n        return compareEvents(event, cursor) &gt; 0;\n      });\n    const selected = matching.slice(0, limit);\n    const items = selected.map(({ id, created_at, type, summary }) =&gt; ({\n      id,\n      created_at,\n      type,\n      summary,\n    }));\n    const nextCursor =\n      matching.length &gt; limit\n        ? encodeCursor(selected.at(-1), tenantId, projectId, signingKey)\n        : null;\n    return send(200, { items, next_cursor: nextCursor });\n  });\n}\n\nexport async function startApi(fixtures, options = {}) {\n  const server = createApi({ ...fixtures, ...options });\n  await new Promise((resolve, reject) =&gt; {\n    server.once(\"error\", reject);\n    server.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", () =&gt; resolve(undefined));\n  });\n  const address = server.address();\n  if (!address || typeof address === \"string\")\n    throw new Error(\"No listening address\");\n  return {\n    baseUrl: `http://127.0.0.1:${address.port}`,\n    close: () =&gt;\n      new Promise((resolve, reject) =&gt;\n        server.close((error) =&gt; (error ? reject(error) : resolve(undefined)))\n      ),\n  };\n}\n</code></pre> </details> <details> <summary>Seeded records and project access fixtures</summary> <pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">export function createFixtures() {\n  const tokenA = randomBytes(24).toString(\"base64url\");\n  const tokenB = randomBytes(24).toString(\"base64url\");\n  const sessions = new Map([\n    [tokenA, \"tenant_a\"],\n    [tokenB, \"tenant_b\"],\n  ]);\n  const projects = new Map([\n    [\"feed\", { tenant_id: \"tenant_a\", name: \"Activity feed\" }],\n    [\"empty\", { tenant_id: \"tenant_a\", name: \"Empty feed\" }],\n    [\"exact\", { tenant_id: \"tenant_a\", name: \"Four events\" }],\n    [\"large\", { tenant_id: \"tenant_a\", name: \"Large feed\" }],\n    [\"precision\", { tenant_id: \"tenant_a\", name: \"Precise timestamps\" }],\n    [\"other\", { tenant_id: \"tenant_a\", name: \"Another project\" }],\n    [\"private\", { tenant_id: \"tenant_b\", name: \"Private project\" }],\n  ]);\n  const event = (id, created_at, project_id, tenant_id = \"tenant_a\") =&gt; ({\n    id,\n    created_at,\n    project_id,\n    tenant_id,\n    type: \"deployment\",\n    summary: `Synthetic event ${id}`,\n    internal_note: \"This field must never enter the HTTP response.\",\n    raw_payload: { synthetic: true },\n  });\n  const feed = [\n    event(\"evt_105\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:03.123456Z\", \"feed\"),\n    event(\"evt_104\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:02.123456Z\", \"feed\"),\n    event(\"evt_103\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:02.123456Z\", \"feed\"),\n    event(\"evt_102\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:02.123456Z\", \"feed\"),\n    event(\"evt_101\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:01.123456Z\", \"feed\"),\n  ];\n  const events = [\n    ...feed,\n    ...feed.slice(0, 4).map((item) =&gt; ({ ...item, project_id: \"exact\" })),\n    ...Array.from({ length: 105 }, (_, index) =&gt;\n      event(\n        `large_${String(index).padStart(3, \"0\")}`,\n        new Date(Date.UTC(2026, 0, 15, 12, 0, index))\n          .toISOString()\n          .replace(\".000Z\", \".123456Z\"),\n        \"large\"\n      )\n    ),\n    // Reverse ID order makes timestamp precision observable in the tests.\n    event(\"precise_a\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:00.123999Z\", \"precision\"),\n    event(\"precise_z\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:00.123001Z\", \"precision\"),\n    event(\"other_1\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:00.123456Z\", \"other\"),\n    event(\"other_2\", \"2026-01-15T11:59:59.123456Z\", \"other\"),\n    event(\"private_1\", \"2026-01-15T12:00:00.123456Z\", \"private\", \"tenant_b\"),\n    event(\"private_2\", \"2026-01-15T11:59:59.123456Z\", \"private\", \"tenant_b\"),\n  ];\n  return {\n    sessions,\n    projects,\n    events,\n    signingKey: randomBytes(32),\n    tokenA,\n    tokenB,\n  };\n}\n</code></pre> </details> <details> <summary>HTTP contract and regression tests</summary> <pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">test(\"five-event traversal crosses a timestamp tie and replays the same continuation\", async () =&gt; {\n  const expected = [\"evt_105\", \"evt_104\", \"evt_103\", \"evt_102\", \"evt_101\"];\n  const pages = await traverse(\"feed\", 2, expected);\n  assert.deepEqual(pages.map(ids), [\n    [\"evt_105\", \"evt_104\"],\n    [\"evt_103\", \"evt_102\"],\n    [\"evt_101\"],\n  ]);\n  assert.equal(pages.length, 3);\n  assert.ok(pages[0].next_cursor);\n  assert.ok(pages[1].next_cursor);\n  assert.equal(pages[2].next_cursor, null);\n  const replay = await request(\"feed\", {\n    limit: \"2\",\n    cursor: pages[0].next_cursor,\n  });\n  assert.deepEqual(replay.body.items, pages[1].items);\n  const next = await request(\"feed\", {\n    limit: \"2\",\n    cursor: replay.body.next_cursor,\n  });\n  assert.deepEqual(next.body.items, pages[2].items);\n  assert.equal(next.body.next_cursor, null);\n  console.log(\n    JSON.stringify({\n      fixture: \"five-event-tie\",\n      pages: pages.map(ids),\n      requests: pages.length,\n      replay: ids(replay.body),\n    })\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"the same tie group traverses correctly with limit three\", async () =&gt; {\n  const pages = await traverse(\"feed\", 3, [\n    \"evt_105\",\n    \"evt_104\",\n    \"evt_103\",\n    \"evt_102\",\n    \"evt_101\",\n  ]);\n  assert.deepEqual(pages.map(ids), [\n    [\"evt_105\", \"evt_104\", \"evt_103\"],\n    [\"evt_102\", \"evt_101\"],\n  ]);\n});\n\ntest(\"timestamp ordering and continuation preserve submillisecond precision\", async () =&gt; {\n  const pages = await traverse(\"precision\", 1, [\"precise_a\", \"precise_z\"]);\n  assert.equal(pages[0].items[0].created_at, \"2026-01-15T12:00:00.123999Z\");\n  assert.equal(pages[1].items[0].created_at, \"2026-01-15T12:00:00.123001Z\");\n});\n\ntest(\"omitted, minimum, and maximum limits return 25, 1, and 100 of 105 events\", async () =&gt; {\n  for (const [parameters, expected] of [\n    [{}, 25],\n    [{ limit: \"1\" }, 1],\n    [{ limit: \"100\" }, 100],\n  ]) {\n    const result = await request(\"large\", parameters);\n    assert.equal(result.status, 200);\n    assert.equal(result.body.items.length, expected);\n    assert.ok(result.body.next_cursor);\n  }\n  const pages = await traverse(\n    \"large\",\n    100,\n    Array.from(\n      { length: 105 },\n      (_, index) =&gt; `large_${String(104 - index).padStart(3, \"0\")}`\n    )\n  );\n  assert.deepEqual(\n    pages.map((page) =&gt; page.items.length),\n    [100, 5]\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"invalid and repeated limits return the documented generic error\", async (context) =&gt; {\n  for (const limit of [\n    \"0\",\n    \"101\",\n    \"-1\",\n    \"1.5\",\n    \"many\",\n    \"\",\n    \"1e2\",\n    \"Infinity\",\n  ]) {\n    await context.test(`limit ${JSON.stringify(limit)}`, async () =&gt; {\n      const result = await request(\"feed\", { limit });\n      assert.equal(result.status, 400);\n      assert.deepEqual(\n        result.body,\n        expectedError(\n          \"invalid_limit\",\n          \"Limit must be an integer from 1 through 100.\"\n        )\n      );\n    });\n  }\n  const repeated = await request(\"feed\", [\n    [\"limit\", \"1\"],\n    [\"limit\", \"2\"],\n  ]);\n  assert.equal(repeated.status, 400);\n});\n\ntest(\"empty, partial, and exactly full final pages have no continuation\", async () =&gt; {\n  assert.deepEqual((await request(\"empty\")).body, {\n    items: [],\n    next_cursor: null,\n  });\n  const partial = await traverse(\"feed\", 2, [\n    \"evt_105\",\n    \"evt_104\",\n    \"evt_103\",\n    \"evt_102\",\n    \"evt_101\",\n  ]);\n  assert.equal(partial.at(-1).items.length, 1);\n  const exact = await traverse(\"exact\", 2, [\n    \"evt_105\",\n    \"evt_104\",\n    \"evt_103\",\n    \"evt_102\",\n  ]);\n  assert.deepEqual(\n    exact.map((page) =&gt; page.items.length),\n    [2, 2]\n  );\n  assert.equal(exact[1].next_cursor, null);\n});\n\ntest(\"authentication precedes malformed and wrong-scope cursor or limit validation\", async () =&gt; {\n  const privateCursor = (\n    await request(\"private\", { limit: \"1\" }, fixtures.tokenB)\n  ).body.next_cursor;\n  for (const token of [null, \"invalid_session\"]) {\n    for (const parameters of [\n      { cursor: \"broken\" },\n      { cursor: privateCursor },\n      { limit: \"0\", cursor: \"broken\" },\n    ]) {\n      const result = await request(\"feed\", parameters, token);\n      assert.equal(result.status, 401);\n      assert.deepEqual(result.body, unauthenticated);\n    }\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"inaccessible and nonexistent projects return identical 404 before cursor validation\", async () =&gt; {\n  const ownCursor = (await request(\"feed\", { limit: \"1\" })).body.next_cursor;\n  for (const project of [\"private\", \"missing\"]) {\n    for (const parameters of [\n      {},\n      { cursor: \"broken\" },\n      { cursor: ownCursor },\n      { limit: \"0\", cursor: \"broken\" },\n    ]) {\n      const result = await request(project, parameters);\n      assert.equal(result.status, 404);\n      assert.deepEqual(result.body, notFound);\n    }\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"a valid cursor from another project in the same tenant is invalid on an authorized feed\", async () =&gt; {\n  const cursor = (await request(\"other\", { limit: \"1\" })).body.next_cursor;\n  assert.ok(cursor);\n  const result = await request(\"feed\", { cursor });\n  assert.equal(result.status, 400);\n  assert.deepEqual(result.body, invalidCursor);\n});\n\ntest(\"a valid cursor from another tenant is invalid on an authorized feed\", async () =&gt; {\n  const cursor = (await request(\"private\", { limit: \"1\" }, fixtures.tokenB))\n    .body.next_cursor;\n  assert.ok(cursor);\n  const result = await request(\"feed\", { cursor });\n  assert.equal(result.status, 400);\n  assert.deepEqual(result.body, invalidCursor);\n});\n\ntest(\"undecodable, empty, tampered, and repeated cursor tokens return the same closed error\", async () =&gt; {\n  const cursor = (await request(\"feed\", { limit: \"1\" })).body.next_cursor;\n  const [payload, signature] = cursor.split(\".\");\n  const tampered = `${payload}.${signature[0] === \"A\" ? \"B\" : \"A\"}${signature.slice(1)}`;\n  for (const token of [\n    \"broken\",\n    \"\",\n    \"%%%.___\",\n    \"a.b.c\",\n    \"x\".repeat(2049),\n    tampered,\n  ]) {\n    const result = await request(\"feed\", { cursor: token });\n    assert.equal(result.status, 400);\n    assert.deepEqual(result.body, invalidCursor);\n  }\n  const result = await request(\"feed\", [\n    [\"cursor\", cursor],\n    [\"cursor\", cursor],\n  ]);\n  assert.equal(result.status, 400);\n  assert.deepEqual(result.body, invalidCursor);\n});\n\ntest(\"signed structurally invalid payloads and unsupported versions are rejected\", async (context) =&gt; {\n  const valid = {\n    version: 1,\n    tenant_id: \"tenant_a\",\n    project_id: \"feed\",\n    created_at: \"2026-01-15T12:00:02.123456Z\",\n    id: \"evt_104\",\n  };\n  const missing = { ...valid };\n  delete missing.id;\n  const cases = [\n    [\"missing ID\", missing],\n    [\"number ID\", { ...valid, id: 104 }],\n    [\"empty ID\", { ...valid, id: \"\" }],\n    [\"number timestamp\", { ...valid, created_at: 0 }],\n    [\"invalid date\", { ...valid, created_at: \"2026-02-30T12:00:00Z\" }],\n    [\"unsupported version\", { ...valid, version: 2 }],\n    [\"extra field\", { ...valid, extra: true }],\n    [\"wrong tenant type\", { ...valid, tenant_id: 1 }],\n    [\"wrong project type\", { ...valid, project_id: null }],\n    [\"null payload\", null],\n    [\"array payload\", []],\n    [\"invalid JSON\", \"not-json\"],\n  ];\n  for (const [name, payload] of cases) {\n    await context.test(name, async () =&gt; {\n      const result = await request(\"feed\", { cursor: signFixture(payload) });\n      assert.equal(result.status, 400);\n      assert.deepEqual(result.body, invalidCursor);\n    });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"every serialized event omits stored tenant, project, and raw payload fields\", async () =&gt; {\n  const result = await request(\"feed\", { limit: \"100\" });\n  assert.equal(result.status, 200);\n  for (const item of result.body.items) {\n    assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(item).sort(), [\n      \"created_at\",\n      \"id\",\n      \"summary\",\n      \"type\",\n    ]);\n  }\n  assert.ok(\n    fixtures.events.some((event) =&gt; event.internal_note &amp;&amp; event.raw_payload)\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"the schema oracle rejects extra, missing, incorrectly typed, and malformed public fields\", () =&gt; {\n  const schema = specification.components.schemas.EventPage;\n  const page = {\n    items: [\n      {\n        id: \"evt_1\",\n        created_at: \"2026-01-15T12:00:00.123456Z\",\n        type: \"deployment\",\n        summary: \"Synthetic\",\n      },\n    ],\n    next_cursor: null,\n  };\n  assert.ok(conforms(page, schema));\n  assert.equal(conforms({ ...page, tenant_id: \"tenant_a\" }, schema), false);\n  assert.equal(\n    conforms(\n      { ...page, items: [{ ...page.items[0], raw_payload: {} }] },\n      schema\n    ),\n    false\n  );\n  assert.equal(conforms({ items: page.items }, schema), false);\n  assert.equal(conforms({ ...page, next_cursor: \"\" }, schema), false);\n  assert.equal(\n    conforms({ ...page, items: [{ ...page.items[0], id: 1 }] }, schema),\n    false\n  );\n  assert.equal(\n    conforms(\n      { ...page, items: [{ ...page.items[0], created_at: \"yesterday\" }] },\n      schema\n    ),\n    false\n  );\n  const errorSchema = specification.components.schemas.InvalidCursor;\n  assert.equal(\n    conforms(\n      { error: { ...invalidCursor.error, stack: \"internal\" } },\n      errorSchema\n    ),\n    false\n  );\n  assert.equal(\n    conforms(\n      { error: { ...invalidCursor.error, message: \"tenant_a\" } },\n      errorSchema\n    ),\n    false\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"the existing project-detail route preserves access and ignores pagination parameters\", async () =&gt; {\n  const own = await request(\n    \"feed\",\n    { cursor: \"broken\", limit: \"0\" },\n    fixtures.tokenA,\n    true\n  );\n  assert.equal(own.status, 200);\n  assert.deepEqual(own.body, { id: \"feed\", name: \"Activity feed\" });\n  const inaccessible = await request(\"private\", {}, fixtures.tokenA, true);\n  assert.equal(inaccessible.status, 404);\n  assert.deepEqual(inaccessible.body, notFound);\n  const unauthenticatedResult = await request(\"feed\", {}, null, true);\n  assert.equal(unauthenticatedResult.status, 401);\n  assert.deepEqual(unauthenticatedResult.body, unauthenticated);\n});\n\ntest(\"OpenAPI declares operation, limit boundaries, signed cursor, and response statuses\", () =&gt; {\n  assert.equal(specification.openapi, \"3.1.0\");\n  const operation = specification.paths[\"/v1/projects/{project_id}/events\"].get;\n  assert.equal(operation.operationId, \"listProjectEvents\");\n  const limit = operation.parameters.find(\n    (parameter) =&gt; parameter.name === \"limit\"\n  ).schema;\n  assert.deepEqual(limit, {\n    type: \"integer\",\n    minimum: 1,\n    maximum: 100,\n    default: 25,\n  });\n  assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(operation.responses).sort(), [\n    \"200\",\n    \"400\",\n    \"401\",\n    \"404\",\n  ]);\n  assert.equal(\n    specification.components.securitySchemes.session.scheme,\n    \"bearer\"\n  );\n});\n</code></pre> </details> <details> <summary>Evidence capture</summary> <pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">mkdirSync(output, { recursive: true });\nconst states = [];\nfor (const [name, arguments_] of [\n  [\"red\", [\"--seeded\"]],\n  [\"green\", []],\n]) {\n  const result = spawnSync(\n    process.execPath,\n    [resolve(directory, \"test.mjs\"), ...arguments_],\n    {\n      cwd: directory,\n      encoding: \"utf8\",\n      timeout: 30_000,\n    }\n  );\n  writeFileSync(\n    resolve(output, `${name}.log`),\n    `${result.stdout ?? \"\"}${result.stderr ?? \"\"}`\n  );\n  states.push({\n    name,\n    command: `node test.mjs${arguments_.length ? \" --seeded\" : \"\"}`,\n    exit_code: result.status,\n    signal: result.signal,\n    error: result.error?.message ?? null,\n  });\n}\nconst sources = Object.fromEntries(\n  readdirSync(directory, { withFileTypes: true })\n    .filter((entry) =&gt; entry.isFile())\n    .map((entry) =&gt; [\n      entry.name,\n      createHash(\"sha256\")\n        .update(readFileSync(resolve(directory, entry.name)))\n        .digest(\"hex\"),\n    ])\n);\nconst observed = { red: await observe(true), green: await observe(false) };\nwriteJson(\"observed-http.json\", observed);\nwriteJson(\"run-manifest.json\", {\n  execution: \"Synthetic loopback HTTP fixture; no external service\",\n  recorded_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n  node: process.version,\n  minimum_node: \"22.6.0\",\n  dependencies: \"Node standard library only; no install step\",\n  baseline:\n    \"Deliberately seeded timestamp-only continuation; not a historical customer defect\",\n  correction:\n    \"Descending timestamp-and-ID tuple continuation using full fractional precision\",\n  source_sha256: sources,\n  states,\n});\nif (\n  states[0].exit_code === null ||\n  states[0].exit_code === 0 ||\n  states[1].exit_code !== 0\n) {\n  throw new Error(\n    \"Expected the unchanged tests to fail on the seeded baseline and pass on the corrected implementation. Inspect red.log and green.log.\"\n  );\n}\nconsole.log(\n  JSON.stringify(\n    {\n      execution: \"synthetic-loopback-http\",\n      red_exit: states[0].exit_code,\n      green_exit: states[1].exit_code,\n      green_pages: observed.green.pages.map((page) =&gt;\n        page.body.items.map((item) =&gt; item.id)\n      ),\n      evidence_directory: output,\n    },\n    null,\n    2\n  )\n);\n</code></pre> </details> <h2 id=\"prepare-the-input-packet\">Prepare the input packet</h2> <p>An issue link is useful only if Codex can read it. Paste or attach the relevant content when the source is unavailable. Include the following information with the starter prompt.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Input</th> <th>Sample issue</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Issue and outcome</td> <td><code>API-142</code>: Add <code>GET /v1/projects/{project_id}/events</code> so customers can page through an activity feed.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Repository and base</td> <td>Put the sample folder in your chosen repository, then record the branch and exact commit selected for the task.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Relevant code</td> <td>The sample's <code>api.mjs</code>, <code>fixtures.mjs</code>, <code>test.mjs</code>, and <code>openapi.json</code>, plus your repository's <code>AGENTS.md</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Existing patterns</td> <td>Keep authentication and project authorization before pagination validation. Use signed cursors and the documented public error envelope. When adapting the issue, follow your repository's existing helpers.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Test setup</td> <td>Fixed in-memory test projects for two tenants, six tenant-A projects, a timestamp tie split across a page boundary, timestamps with fractional precision, empty and exactly full final pages, and 105 events for limit checks.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Validation</td> <td><code>node test.mjs --seeded</code> (expected failure), <code>node test.mjs</code> (corrected state), and <code>node reproduce.mjs ./evidence</code>. Run <code>node --check</code> for each <code>.mjs</code> file. For your own service, add its actual type, lint, regression, and CI commands.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Scope</td> <td>Endpoint, focused tests, and its OpenAPI documentation. No new dependencies, database migration, frontend, deployment, or auth redesign.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Handoff</td> <td>A draft PR when the available repository integration supports it and you have authorized creation; otherwise a diff and draft PR description.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>For the sample, prepare Node 22.6 or later; the tests create their own test sessions and cursor-signing key and bind a temporary HTTP server to the loopback interface. For your own service, also prepare its dependencies, test configuration, and isolated services. Verify that its cursor helper can bind a cursor to the authenticated tenant and requested project before assigning this issue.</p> <h3 id=\"define-the-api-contract\">Define the API contract</h3> <p>Confirm the sample contract below matches your repository before implementation. A successful response is HTTP 200 with exactly <code>{ items, next_cursor }</code>.</p> <p>Each item has exactly four required public fields: <code>id</code> (nonempty string), <code>created_at</code> (UTC RFC 3339 timestamp string), <code>type</code> (nonempty string), and <code>summary</code> (string). <code>items</code> is an array of these objects; <code>next_cursor</code> is an opaque nonempty string or <code>null</code>.</p> <p>Internal tenant/project keys, database metadata, raw event payloads, and credentials are not response fields. Describe response field types, required fields, whether fields allow <code>null</code>, and closed object shapes in OpenAPI. Verify the serialized HTTP bodies against that schema.</p> <p>Events sort by <code>created_at DESC, id DESC</code>, preserving the timestamp's fractional precision and using descending lexical ID order. The cursor resumes strictly after the last returned tuple in that order.</p> <p>The default page size is 25; valid limits are decimal integers from 1 through 100. Repeated limit or cursor parameters are invalid. Return a non-null cursor only when another matching event exists.</p> <p>Both a partial final page and an exactly full final page return <code>next_cursor: null</code>; an empty authorized project returns <code>items: []</code> and <code>next_cursor: null</code>.</p> <p>The sample signs each cursor and binds it to the authenticated tenant and requested project. Authenticate and authorize the requested project before validating its limit or cursor, so parameter errors cannot reveal whether another tenant's project exists.</p> <p>A missing or invalid session returns 401; an inaccessible or nonexistent project returns the same generic 404. After confirming access, check the limit before the cursor.</p> <p>A malformed, tampered, structurally invalid, or tenant/project-mismatched cursor returns HTTP 400 with code <code>invalid_cursor</code>. A valid cursor for another project in the same tenant, or for another tenant, is invalid when supplied to an authorized project.</p> <p>A supplied cursor must not change the authorization result for an inaccessible project. The sample's version-1 cursor does not expire; unsupported versions are invalid.</p> <p>In the sample, every error body has exactly <code>{ error: { code, message } }</code>, with both fields required strings and no extra fields.</p> <p>Use these generic error responses:</p> <ul> <li>400 <code>invalid_cursor</code> / <code>Invalid cursor.</code></li> <li>400 <code>invalid_limit</code> / <code>Limit must be an integer from 1 through 100.</code></li> <li>401 <code>unauthenticated</code> / <code>Authentication required.</code></li> <li>404 <code>not_found</code> / <code>Project not found.</code></li> </ul> <p>Keep decoded cursor contents, tenant/project identifiers, raw errors, and stack traces out of every error body. Use the real repository's approved envelope and codes if they differ; resolve that contract difference before changing shared helpers.</p> <p>Traversal and replay assertions use fixed fixtures with no concurrent writes: following cursors returns every event once in the agreed order and terminates within <code>ceil(event_count / limit)</code> requests for a nonempty feed, or one request for an empty feed.</p> <p>Replaying a valid cursor with the same request parameters returns the same items and continuation position while those fixtures stay unchanged; it need not produce byte-identical signed tokens.</p> <p>This contract does not promise single-use cursors, snapshot pagination, or identical results after feed changes. Document the repository's existing feed consistency policy; stop for a product decision if no policy exists and the issue requires snapshot behavior.</p> <h2 id=\"how-to-use\">How to use</h2> <ol> <li><strong>Choose the issue and prepare the environment.</strong> Confirm that the contract above matches the actual repository. Select the prepared cloud environment and the intended base commit. Supply the issue packet directly in the task; starting this recipe does not depend on an automatic issue-tracker trigger.</li> <li><strong>Run the starter prompt.</strong> Replace its bracketed inputs with your repository, issue packet, boundaries, and checks. Choose whether Codex should return a diff or create an authorized draft PR. The starter prompt on this page contains the full handoff instructions.</li> <li><strong>Establish the baseline.</strong> Codex should read repository instructions and run the approved baseline checks before editing.</li> </ol> <p>For the sample, run <code>node test.mjs</code> and the syntax checks in <code>README.md</code>; <code>--seeded</code> is a separate deliberate failure demonstration.</p> <p>For your own service, run its existing regression, type, and lint checks. A new endpoint's focused test file may not exist yet; record that as a test to create. Resolve failing existing checks or unavailable test services before attributing later results to the feature.</p> <ol> <li><strong>Implement and verify the contract.</strong> Ask Codex to use the existing access and cursor helpers, implement the endpoint, add the acceptance tests below, and update its API documentation. Where practical, the new tests should fail against the original code and pass after the change. Keep those results with the final verification record. In the downloadable sample, <code>--seeded</code> selects a deliberate defect for this comparison; this comparison is separate from a failing baseline in your repository.</li> <li><strong>Review the change and its evidence.</strong> Read the diff, acceptance checks, check outputs, and remaining risks together. If Codex creates an authorized draft PR, verify that its base and head are correct. If PR tooling is unavailable, use the returned diff and description to prepare the PR through your normal process. List any unresolved checks in the draft PR and keep it unready for merge.</li> <li><strong>Resolve review feedback and merge through your normal process.</strong> Give Codex the specific comments to address in the same task, then rerun the affected checks. A reviewer confirms required CI and approves the final commit before merging.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"acceptance-tests-to-require\">Acceptance tests to require</h2> <p>These tests make the issue small enough to delegate and specific enough to review. Adapt the names to your test runner, while preserving the behavior each test proves.</p> <h3 id=\"stable-traversal\">Stable traversal</h3> <p>Seed five fixed events: <code>evt_105</code> has the newest timestamp, <code>evt_104</code>, <code>evt_103</code>, and <code>evt_102</code> share the middle timestamp, and <code>evt_101</code> has the oldest.</p> <p>With <code>limit=2</code>, require exactly these pages: <code>[evt_105, evt_104]</code>, <code>[evt_103, evt_102]</code>, <code>[evt_101]</code>. The tie group must cross the first boundary.</p> <p>Assert exact order, no duplicate or missing IDs, non-null cursors on the first two pages, and a null cursor on the third; fail if traversal exceeds three requests.</p> <p>Replay the first continuation cursor with the same limit against unchanged fixtures and assert the same second-page items and continuation position.</p> <h3 id=\"default-and-boundary-sizes\">Default and boundary sizes</h3> <p>Seed more than 100 events. Assert 25 items without a <code>limit</code> parameter, one with <code>limit=1</code>, and 100 with <code>limit=100</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"invalid-limits\">Invalid limits</h3> <p>Assert HTTP 400 for <code>0</code>, <code>101</code>, <code>-1</code>, a fractional value, and a string such as <code>many</code>, using the existing validation error shape.</p> <h3 id=\"empty-and-final-pages\">Empty and final pages</h3> <p>Assert an empty authorized project returns <code>items: []</code> and <code>next_cursor: null</code>. With <code>limit=2</code>, assert that five events produce a one-item third page with a null cursor and that four events produce a two-item second page with a null cursor. The full final page must not require an extra empty request.</p> <h3 id=\"authentication\">Authentication</h3> <p>Assert missing and invalid sessions return the agreed 401 schema, including requests with a malformed cursor or a cursor from another scope. Cursor validation must not override authentication.</p> <h3 id=\"tenant-isolation\">Tenant isolation</h3> <p>Authenticate as tenant A and request tenant B's project or a nonexistent project. Assert the same agreed generic 404 body with no event data, including when the request carries a malformed or mismatched cursor. Authorization must precede cursor validation.</p> <h3 id=\"cursor-scope\">Cursor scope</h3> <p>Request an authorized tenant-A project with (1) a valid signed cursor from another tenant-A project and (2) a valid signed cursor issued under tenant B.</p> <p>Assert both return the same HTTP 400 <code>invalid_cursor</code> body with no event data or scope details. Test these separately from requests to an inaccessible project, which must return 404.</p> <h3 id=\"malformed-and-tampered-cursors\">Malformed and tampered cursors</h3> <p>On an authorized project, assert HTTP 400 <code>invalid_cursor</code> for tokens the helper cannot decode, tokens with modified signatures, and signed tokens that omit required cursor fields or give those fields the wrong type. Use isolated test signing fixtures.</p> <p>Cover unsupported versions or expired tokens if the shared helper supports those features. Assert that responses match the agreed generic error schema and contain no decoded contents, identifiers, raw errors, or stack traces.</p> <h3 id=\"existing-behavior\">Existing behavior</h3> <p>The sample checks the existing project-detail route with authorized, unauthorized, and inaccessible-project requests. Run syntax checks for its <code>.mjs</code> files. In your service, run its established regression suite, type check, and lint.</p> <h3 id=\"public-response-schema\">Public response schema</h3> <p>Validate actual HTTP 200, 400, 401, and 404 response bodies against the agreed OpenAPI schemas. Assert required keys, item field types, timestamp format, whether the cursor allows <code>null</code>, and no extra properties at any object level.</p> <p>Seed internal fields in stored events and verify they are absent from serialized items; verify every error response contains only its approved generic code and message.</p> <h3 id=\"documentation\">Documentation</h3> <p>Verify the OpenAPI operation and examples match the implemented parameters, exact success/error schemas, authorization precedence, ordering, final-page rules, and fixed-fixture replay/consistency limits. Run the repository's API specification validation if one exists.</p> <h2 id=\"what-good-output-looks-like\">What good output looks like</h2> <h3 id=\"shared-evidence-record\">Shared evidence record</h3> <p>Use this evidence format for each acceptance criterion. Populate it from observed output. For a new test that does not exist at baseline, distinguish “not yet present” from a failed existing check.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Criterion / test: [specific behavior and test location]\nEnvironment: [published setup reference; runtime, database and dependency versions]\nBefore: [revision + test-only diff ID; command; exit code; observed assertion; log path]\nAfter: [final revision or base + diff ID; command; exit code; observed assertion; log path]\nStatus: [pass / fail / blocked / not run]\nLimits / reviewer action: [untested behavior, blocker, or decision required]\n</code></pre> <p>Keep red and green runs tied to their actual tested states, including test-only changes on the original revision. Keep the logs, response fixtures, and final diff with the handoff; file and test names alone do not prove execution. Update the evidence when the tested revision changes. Checks that are blocked or have not run cannot count as passing.</p> <p>A useful PR description links each claim to its evidence. Use this handoff template and replace every bracketed field with observed results.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Title: Add cursor pagination for project events\nIssue: API-142\nBase: [branch and commit]\nTested state: [head commit, or base commit plus attached diff identifier]\n\nChanges\n- Add the project-events endpoint using the existing project access helper.\n- Reuse signed cursors scoped to tenant and project.\n- Add contract tests and update the OpenAPI operation.\n\nAcceptance evidence\n- [One row per criterion above: test, observed result, and log reference.]\n\nValidation\n- Before edits: [command, result, and log reference for each baseline check].\n- New tests against original code: [result, or not run with reason].\n- After edits: [command, result, and log reference for each required check].\n- CI: [check links and actual states, or not available].\n- Remaining checks: [specific checks and blockers, or none with supporting evidence].\n\nReviewer focus\n- [Highest-risk behavior and unresolved criteria.]\n\nRemaining risk and rollback\n- [Observed limitations; distinguish them from untested assumptions.]\n- [How this change can be reverted and whether any callers depend on it.]\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"iterate-from-review-comments\">Iterate from review comments</h2> <p>Use a focused follow-up for a specific review finding. For example:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Address this review comment in the current change:\n\"Repeat the five-event traversal with limit=3; assert pages\n[evt_105, evt_104, evt_103] and [evt_102, evt_101], then a null cursor.\"\n\nAdd the regression test and change the implementation only if it exposes a\nfailure. Rerun the focused endpoint tests and any other required checks affected\nby the edit. Update the evidence table with the tested state and actual results.\nKeep the same scope. Do not merge or deploy.\n</code></pre> <p>Provide the text of the comment if Codex cannot access the review directly. A reviewer should check that the response resolves the behavior in question, rather than only satisfying the wording of the comment.</p> <h2 id=\"when-to-stop\">When to stop</h2> <ul> <li><strong>The baseline is red or cannot run.</strong> Return the failing check and setup details. Fix the environment or agree on a documented baseline before continuing.</li> <li><strong>The contract conflicts with existing behavior.</strong> Identify the conflict, affected callers, and the smallest decision needed. Do not silently change the contract.</li> <li><strong>The change needs a migration, new dependency, or auth redesign.</strong> Explain why and split or re-scope the issue before expanding it.</li> <li><strong>Tests fail after implementation.</strong> Do not treat the change as ready to merge. Report the failing cases. Do not remove assertions or weaken authorization to make checks pass.</li> <li><strong>Repository write integration is unavailable.</strong> Return the diff, draft PR description, and validation evidence. A teammate can complete the repository handoff.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"reuse-the-workflow\">Reuse the workflow</h2> <p>After a reviewer accepts the first result, save the issue packet and acceptance checklist in your team's issue template. Record stable repository guidance, such as test commands and where API contracts live, in <code>AGENTS.md</code> or the existing contributor guide.</p>"};
